  "testbench": {
    "name": "comparator-transient-noise",
    "description": "Input-referred noise floor of the WHOLE comparator (comparator_dut, the real regenerative latch, NOT comparator_dut_analog), measured by transient-noise decision statistics (a 'hit-rate' / probit measurement) over the full PVT grid -- the compliance evidence path CLAUDE.md requires and DR-0002 (issue #12 / PR #18, PROPOSED AND STILL OPEN at the time this bench was built) proposes to ratify, per CLAUDE.md's 'input-referred noise floor from transient-noise runs with seeds and run counts committed'. The injected trnoise() source is calibrated to the SPECTRAL DENSITY of comparator-preamp-noise's own input-referred white noise (36.27 nV/rtHz at the nominal corner), NOT to that bench's band-limited integrated total -- the latch's own aperture, not the reduced sub-model's bandwidth, then sets the noise bandwidth that reaches the decision.",
    "claim": "sim/dut.json binds design/comparator.spice (id comparator-dr0001, provenance schematic), the ratified topology from spec/decision-records/0001-comparator-topology.md ('DR-0001'). This record substantiates a TRNOISE-injected, decision-statistics sweep over the full PVT grid against the WHOLE latch (comparator_dut, real CLK strobe, real regenerative pair): at each PVT point it measures the probability of a correct decision at +/- a fixed differential overdrive, from which an input-referred 1-sigma decision noise follows by probit inversion (see this experiment's README.md). It is NOT itself the README.md#target-specification Input-referred-noise row ratification act (that is spec/porting-plan.md's separate third step; DR-0002, issue #12 / PR #18, would ratify the SCOPING of the row and name transient noise as its compliance evidence path -- but that PR is OPEN AND UNRATIFIED on main at the time this record is committed, so nothing here is measured against a ratified bound; the requirement this bench actually answers to is CLAUDE.md's own, which is in force today). Unlike comparator-preamp-noise/'s .noise analysis, this bench exercises the ACTUAL regenerative loop -- no loop-broken reduced sub-model, no small-signal DC-operating-point assumption, and no reliance on that sub-model's own noise bandwidth. It remains a LOWER BOUND on the complete figure in one specific, stated way: the DUT's black-box pin contract lets this deck inject noise only at vinp/vinn, so the regenerative pair's own noise sources are not independently sourced (see the notes below).",
    "experiment": "comparator-transient-noise",
    "directory": "testbench",
    "netlist": "tb_transient_noise.spice",
    "netlist_sha256": "8cd004296a2f6f63ef7196ef19454eaf4e6225f059d28982c92a1b4342157f75",
    "manifest_sha256": "b8e42b7d0836961feed4d88ce9031543b2554a8282d1ad445018af875cefa728",
    "nominal_supply_v": 1.2,
    "supply_tolerance": 0.1
  },
  "checks": {
    "frac_high_zero": {
      "min": 0.1,
      "max": 0.9,
      "description": "NOISE-IS-ACTUALLY-INJECTED GUARD, not a spec bound. At zero applied overdrive, zero mismatch (the plain mos corner set), the ONLY thing that can make a trial decide either way is the injected trnoise() realization -- so frac_high_zero should sit near 0.5 (binomial SEM at N=80 is ~5.6% at p=0.5). If trnoise() ever failed to inject (e.g. a regression that zeroed vn_na), the zero-overdrive rung would instead decide the SAME way on EVERY trial, collapsing frac_high_zero to 0.0 or 1.0 -- well outside this floor/ceiling. THIS IS NOT AN ASSUMPTION, IT WAS RUN: with vn_na forced to 0 at tt_27c_1.20v this deck returns frac_high_zero = 2.3e-8 (LOW on every trial), frac_high_plus = 1.0 and frac_high_minus = 2.3e-8, and this check FAILS as designed -- see this experiment's README.md 'Negative control (actually run)'. THIS IS ALSO THE HARNESS'S SABOTAGE-NEGATIVE-CONTROL SURROGATE FOR THIS BENCH: --sabotage-corners forces every corner to plain mos_tt (sim/harness/corners.py), which does not itself disable trnoise() the way it disables mismatch for comparator-offset-mc/, so this check's real teeth are structural (a broken or zeroed noise source), not sabotage-corner-specific."
    },
    "frac_high_plus": {
      "min": 0.3,
      "max": 0.999,
      "description": "SANITY ENVELOPE, not a spec bound. At +od_x (1.0 mV, deliberately chosen near the measured 1-sigma decision noise so the hit rate lands in the informative 0.7-0.95 band rather than saturating) the correct decision is HIGH, so frac_high_plus should sit above 0.5. The floor is loose (0.3) so N=80 sampling variance cannot fail an otherwise-fine point, while still catching a badly broken or inverted-polarity deck (frac_high_plus stuck near 0 across the WHOLE grid). The ceiling is 0.999, not 1.0, on purpose: a saturated frac_high_plus = 1.0 carries no information about sigma (the probit inversion of p=1 is infinite, so sigma would read as exactly 0), so saturation is a measurement failure for this bench and must fail the check rather than silently produce a flattering number."
    },
    "frac_high_minus": {
      "min": 0.001,
      "max": 0.7,
      "description": "SANITY ENVELOPE, symmetric with frac_high_plus above: at -od_x the correct decision is LOW, so frac_high_minus (the fraction deciding HIGH, i.e. INCORRECTLY) should sit below 0.5. Ceiling loosened to 0.7 for the same N=80 sampling-variance reason; the 0.001 floor is the mirror of the 0.999 ceiling above -- a saturated frac_high_minus = 0 inverts to an infinite probit and a sigma of exactly 0, which is a measurement failure, not a pass."
    }
  },
